\details{
Datetimes are commonly stored as numeric values in databases (e.g. SQLite
keeps seconds since the epoch), so filter bounds are sent to the database as
numbers.

Following the `tblist` implementation, `cb_get_filter_stats` reports `min`,
`max` and the frequency bounds as numeric seconds since the epoch, whereas
`cb_domain_from_data` returns `POSIXct` values (coerced with [as.POSIXct()]
